1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,600
A flow policy makes each action chunk by integrating an ODE over many steps.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:09,600
A DDPG-style update must push the critic gradient back through every step.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:15,800
Memory grows with the step count, and the Jacobian product can explode or vanish.

4
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:20,800
Value-conditioning (RA-BC, AWR, RECAP) reweights the demonstrations.

5
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:25,400
It stays within the demonstrations and cannot synthesize new actions.

6
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:30,000
Auxiliary modules (DSRL, PLD, RLT) freeze the flow and learn its noise or a residual.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,600
The base policy is never updated, so the adapter caps the headroom.

8
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:39,200
Adjoint methods (QAM) turn the critic gradient into a target at every ODE step.

9
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:44,000
But the critic is queried at generated actions, so its errors reach every step.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,600
FlowDPG queries the critic once, at an in-distribution estimate, with no backprop through the ODE.

11
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:55,200
A training sample pairs noise x₀ with a demo action x₁; xₜ lies between them.

12
00:00:55,200 --> 00:01:00,600
One forward pass projects xₜ to a clean-action estimate, â.

13
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:06,200
The critic gradient at â is rescaled to the local velocity: the adaptive shift.

14
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:12,000
The shifted action a* gives a new target u* = a* − x₀, fit with one L2 loss.

15
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,800
A BC anchor keeps actions feasible. Deployment stays a plain ODE solve.

16
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:22,400
The FlowDPG gradient is vanilla DPG under three explicit approximations.

17
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:27,600
Critic at â, so ODE sensitivity is the identity; one sampled t; a normalized step.

18
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:32,800
A consistency loss keeps â near the true endpoint, where the critic is reliable.

19
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:39,000
Offline: backbone, twin-critic IQL and flow actor train together on demonstrations.

20
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,800
Online: the robot collects rollouts while critic and actor update asynchronously.
